From 8c8045f0c22b6d0db9d5bff3a81b29de88583f0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:42:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: Access Point, Media Bridge and Router run Reaper's own
 step page

Changing the operation mode to Access Point, Media Bridge or back to
Router sent the shell to the stock QIS wizard (QIS_wizard.htm flag=lanip,
sitesurvey_mb, rtMode). Reaper_ModeSetup.asp?mode=ap|mb|rt replaces those
three hand-offs and writes exactly what the stock QIS_V3 wizard writes on
this platform (handler.js goTo.apMode / mbMode / rtMode; plugins.js
setupWLCNvram, handle_mld_enable, getRestartService): sw_mode, wlc_*,
cfg_master, the LAN step (DHCP or static), mld_enable, restart_all for
Router and reboot otherwise. The Media Bridge parent list comes from the
Site Survey engine (reaper_wifi.cgi). The page is skip-listed in
reaper_inject.c: its own theme, top level, it ends in a restart. The
chooser's WISP branch (sw_mode 6) is gone - RTCONFIG_WISP is unset on the
roster. The MLO page's "Get started" opens the Wireless console instead
of the wizard. Repeater and AiMesh Node still use the stock wizard.
Strings RMOD_1..85 are in the packs commit. Lean: test_mode_setup.py,
the qis-no-entry static check (sub-check 7), four markers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
