+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<!--
+	Reaper_ModeSetup.asp - operation-mode step page (rung B of docs/backlog/qis-aimesh-only.md, 2026-10-15).
+
+	Replaces the stock wizard hand-off from Advanced_OperationMode_Content.asp for
+	Access Point, Media Bridge and the return to Router. Repeater and AiMesh Node
+	still go to the stock wizard. Entered as /Reaper_ModeSetup.asp?mode=ap|mb|rt.
+
+	WHAT IT WRITES is exactly what the stock QIS_V3 wizard writes on this
+	platform (bcmwifi + amas + mlo), read from www/sysdep/FUNCTION/QIS_V3/mobile/js:
+	  ap  handler.js goTo.apMode: sw_mode=3 wlc_psta=0 wlc_dpsta=0 mlo_rp=0 mlo_mb=0
+	      cfg_master=1, then the LAN step (lanDHCP / apply.lanStatic).
+	  mb  goTo.mbMode: sw_mode=3 wlc_psta=1 wlc_dpsta=0 cfg_master=0; the parent
+	      from plugins.js setupWLCNvram() folded by transformWLCObj() into wlc_*;
+	      generalObj (x_Setting w_Setting qis_Setting = 1); the LAN step.
+	  rt  goTo.rtMode: sw_mode=1 wlc_psta=0 wlc_dpsta=0 wlc_band="" mlo_rp=0 mlo_mb=0
+	      cfg_master=1 and, as the advSetting + mode-change branch does, the LAN
+	      back to static lan_ipaddr_rt / lan_netmask_rt with DNS cleared.
+	  mld_enable follows plugins.js handle_mld_enable(): RT/AP take the default on
+	      a mode change, MB forces 0.
+	  service: plugins.js getRestartService(): restart_all for a change to
+	      Router, reboot for every other mode change.
+	The AP flow does not run the wizard's Wi-Fi step: the router keeps its
+	networks (they live in the main SDN profile on this build). The Router flow
+	does not run the WAN wizard either: the WAN page owns WAN settings.
+
+	The stock wizard's parent password pre-check (start_wpasupp_qis) is a no-op
+	on a configured box: rc's wpasupp_qis sets every wpasN_reason to "completed"
+	unless x_Setting=0 or the box is already a client. So there is none here, and
+	the page says the password is only tried after the restart.
+
+	Parent list: Reaper's survey engine (reaper_wifi.cgi svystart / svydata, the
+	Site Survey page's backend), not restart_wlcscan + get_ap_info.
+
+	Save: one POST to applyapp.cgi, the endpoint httpApi.nvramSet uses for the
+	wizard. A reboot can cut the reply, so the overlay starts on success AND on
+	error (reaper-ui rule 47); nvramSet would call back on success only. Top-level, own theme: reaper_skip[] in httpd/reaper_inject.c.
+	i18n: RMOD_* plus reused stock tokens, only in backtick strings (rule 29).
+	ASCII only (rule 1).
+-->
